        "# Index\n",
        "\n",
        "An index identifies a position in an ordered sequence. Python sequence indices start at zero; negative indices count from the end, so `items[-1]` selects the last item.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: [Python glossary](https://docs.python.org/3/glossary.html#term-index)"
      ]
    }
